      "Bash(git commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\ntooling: add Makefile and PowerShell helpers for docs\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git push -u origin tooling/dx-make-scripts)",
      "Bash(gh pr create --title \"tooling: add Makefile and PowerShell helpers for docs\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\nAdds cross-platform tooling shortcuts for docs workflows, making it easier to validate docs and sync diagram wrappers on both Windows and Linux/CI.\n\n### New Files\n\n**PowerShell Scripts (Windows-friendly):**\n- `tooling/scripts/docs_check.ps1` - Runs docs validation\n- `tooling/scripts/diagrams_sync.ps1` - Syncs diagram wrappers and validates\n\n**Makefile (cross-platform):**\n- `Makefile` - Provides `make` targets for docs workflows:\n  - `make docs-check` - Run docs validation\n  - `make diagrams-sync` - Sync diagram wrappers and validate\n\n### Updated Files\n\n**Documentation:**\n- `docs/handbooks/obsidian.md` - Added \"Developer Shortcuts\" section documenting both PowerShell and make commands\n\n### Usage\n\n**On Windows (PowerShell):**\n```powershell\n./tooling/scripts/docs_check.ps1\n./tooling/scripts/diagrams_sync.ps1\n```\n\n**Cross-platform (make):**\n```bash\nmake docs-check\nmake diagrams-sync\n```\n\n### Benefits\n- 🪟 **Windows-native:** PowerShell scripts work out-of-the-box on Windows\n- 🐧 **CI-ready:** Makefile works on Linux CI environments\n- 🎯 **Simple commands:** No need to remember Python paths or script locations\n- 📝 **Self-documenting:** Commands are easy to discover and use\n\n### Design Decisions\n- PowerShell scripts use hardcoded Python path for Office3 Windows environment\n- Makefile uses `PY ?= python` variable for flexibility (override with `make PY=python3`)\n- Both approaches call the same underlying Python scripts\n\n### Validation\n- ✅ Docs validation passed\n- ✅ All shortcuts point to correct scripts\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git switch -c docs/templates-userstory-adr)",
      "Bash(git switch docs/templates-userstory-adr)",
      "Bash(git commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\ndocs(templates): add User Story and Decision (ADR-lite) Templater templates\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git push -u origin docs/templates-userstory-adr)",
      "Bash(gh pr create --title \"docs(templates): add User Story and Decision (ADR-lite) Templater templates\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\nAdds Templater templates for User Stories and Decision Records (ADR-lite) to streamline documentation creation in Obsidian.\n\n### New Files\n\n**Templater Templates:**\n- `docs/_templates/user-story.md` - User Story template with standard structure\n- `docs/_templates/decision.md` - Decision Record (ADR-lite) template\n\n### Updated Files\n\n**Documentation Index:**\n- `docs/README.md` - Added \"Templates\" section with links to both templates\n\n### Template Features\n\n**User Story Template (`user-story.md`):**\n- Auto-generates ID from file title (kebab-case)\n- Dynamic front-matter with current date\n- Standard user story format:\n  - As a … (actor/role)\n  - I want … (capability/feature)\n  - So that … (business value)\n- Acceptance Criteria (Gherkin format)\n- Dependencies and Links sections\n\n**Decision Record Template (`decision.md`):**\n- Auto-generates ID from file title (kebab-case)\n- Dynamic front-matter with current date\n- ADR-lite structure:\n  - Context\n  - Options Considered (A, B, C)\n  - Decision (chosen option + rationale)\n  - Consequences (positive/negative)\n  - Links section\n\n### Usage in Obsidian\n\n1. Create a new file with desired title\n2. Insert template using Templater command\n3. Templater auto-fills:\n   - `id` - derived from filename\n   - `title` - from filename\n   - `last_validated` - today''s date\n4. Fill in remaining sections\n\n### Template Structure\n\nBoth templates include:\n- ✅ Valid front-matter for CI validation (satisfies validator)\n- ✅ Templater code block with dynamic field generation\n- ✅ Second front-matter block (generated output for new docs)\n- ✅ Structured content sections with placeholders\n\n### Validation\n- ✅ Docs CI validation passed\n- ✅ Templates include proper front-matter\n- ✅ Linked from docs/README.md for discoverability\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git switch -c docs/ci-badge)",
      "Bash(git switch docs/ci-badge)",
      "Bash(git add docs/README.md)",
      "Bash(git commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\ndocs: add Docs CI status badge to docs/README.md\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git push -u origin docs/ci-badge)",
      "Bash(gh pr create --title \"docs: add Docs CI status badge to docs/README.md\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\nAdds a GitHub Actions status badge to the docs README to display the current Docs CI workflow status.\n\n### Changes\n\n**docs/README.md:**\n- Added CI badge line immediately after front-matter, before the main heading\n- Badge URL: `https://github.com/kentonium3/kg-automation/actions/workflows/docs-ci.yml/badge.svg`\n- Alt text: \"Docs CI\"\n\n### Badge Display\n\nThe badge shows:\n- ✅ **Green (passing):** All docs validation checks pass\n- ❌ **Red (failing):** Docs validation has errors\n- ⚪ **Gray (no status):** No recent runs\n\n### Benefits\n- 📊 **At-a-glance status:** See docs health immediately when viewing README\n- 🔗 **Clickable:** Badge links to workflow runs on GitHub Actions\n- 🎯 **Standard practice:** Aligns with common OSS repository conventions\n\n### Validation\n- ✅ Docs CI validation passed locally\n- ✅ Badge URL verified against actual workflow filename\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git switch -c claude/preset-doc-hygiene)",
      "Bash(git switch claude/preset-doc-hygiene)",
      "Bash(git commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\nclaude: add ''doc-hygiene'' preset and docs\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git push -u origin claude/preset-doc-hygiene)",
      "Bash(git switch -c docs/vision-and-schemas)",
      "Bash(git switch docs/vision-and-schemas)",
      "Bash(git commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\ndocs: add vision framework, machine schemas, and governance templates\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\")",
      "Bash(git push -u origin docs/vision-and-schemas)",
      "Bash(gh pr create --title \"docs: add vision framework, machine schemas, and governance templates\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\nAdds foundational strategy documentation, machine-readable schemas for capabilities and services, and governance templates to establish the vision and operational framework.\n\n### New Files Created\n\n**Strategy (Human-Facing):**\n- `docs/strategy/vision-framework.md` - Canonical vision and conceptual framework document\n  - Placeholder for full vision content\n  - Includes machine note for agent alignment\n\n**Capabilities Schema (Machine-Facing):**\n- `systems/capabilities/schema.json` - JSON Schema for capability definitions\n  - Required fields: id, name, status, owners, inputs, outputs\n  - Optional: description, dependencies, docs, tags\n  - Status values: proposed, planned, in_progress, live, deprecated\n- `systems/capabilities/examples/content-pipeline.json` - Example capability instance\n\n**Product Catalog Schema (Machine-Facing):**\n- `systems/catalog/schema.json` - JSON Schema for external services/products\n  - Required fields: id, name, category, capabilities, auth\n  - Auth types: oauth, api_key, basic, none\n- `systems/catalog/examples/github.json` - Example service instance\n\n**Governance Templates (Human-Facing):**\n- `workflows/project-charter.md` - Template for project charters\n  - Sections: Problem/Opportunity, Outcomes, Scope, Stakeholders, Metrics, Milestones, Risks\n- `workflows/decision-log.md` - Append-only decision log template\n  - Format: Date, Context, Options, Decision, Consequences, Links\n- `workflows/risk-register.md` - Risk tracking table template\n  - Columns: ID, Risk, Likelihood, Impact, Owner, Mitigation, Status\n\n### Updated Files\n\n**Documentation Index:**\n- `docs/README.md` - Added three new top-level sections:\n  - **Strategy:** Vision & Conceptual Framework\n  - **Machine Schemas:** Capabilities and Product Catalog schemas\n  - **Governance:** Project Charter, Decision Log, Risk Register\n\n### Schema Design\n\n**Capabilities Schema:**\nDefines system capabilities with clear inputs/outputs and dependency tracking.\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"cap-content-pipeline\",\n  \"name\": \"Content Pipeline\",\n  \"status\": \"planned\",\n  \"owners\": [\"@kentonium3\"],\n  \"inputs\": [\"user-stories\", \"research-notes\"],\n  \"outputs\": [\"drafts\", \"approved-assets\"],\n  \"dependencies\": [\"cap-claude-code-exec\"]\n}\n```\n\n**Product Catalog Schema:**\nCatalogs external services with authentication and capability info.\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"svc-github\",\n  \"name\": \"GitHub\",\n  \"category\": \"VCS/CI\",\n  \"capabilities\": [\"pull_requests\", \"actions\"],\n  \"auth\": { \"type\": \"oauth\", \"scopes\": [\"repo\"] }\n}\n```\n\n### Benefits\n- 📋 **Strategic Foundation:** Vision framework establishes canonical direction\n- 🤖 **Machine-Readable:** JSON schemas enable programmatic validation and tooling\n- 📊 **Governance Structure:** Templates standardize project and risk management\n- 🔗 **Agent Alignment:** Machine note in vision doc ensures agent compliance\n- ✅ **Validated:** All docs pass CI validation\n\n### Validation\n- ✅ Docs CI validation passed\n- ✅ All front-matter includes required fields\n- ✅ JSON schemas follow JSON Schema Draft 2020-12\n- ✅ doc_type corrected to ''reference'' (not ''guide'')\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\")",
